o -4.4, a 12.0-point loss and the worst move of the game. The engine wanted B7."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "F9 lost 11.5 points, from +0.1 to -11.4, with the engine preferring C8. Black got the stones around E9 and F8, but not the corner fight on the left."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "The 14k's B8 lost 11.4 points and put the lead back to +0.0, with the engine choosing B9. Black had a chance to take the game back."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "C8 turned +3.4 into -7.5, a 10.9-point loss (the engine's choice was A4). Black was ahead before the move, and after it the left side belonged to White. From there the lead never came back."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a board pasted on stdin and prints each group's stones and liberties (flood fill, no move generation or lookahead), and the other commands just read and appended to the games.md game log, so nothing chose or ranked moves.", "stop": false}}